 "result": "Everything is in `src/tessel/cli.py`:\n\n- **Decorator:** `@needs_app_scope` (`src/tessel/cli.py:380`). It gets the app from `LaunchInfo`, loads it if needed, and pushes `app.app_context()` before your command runs.\n- **Class that loads the app:** `LaunchInfo` (`src/tessel/cli.py:293`). Its `load_app()` method (`src/tessel/cli.py:333`) finds and returns the `Tessel` app.\n\nYou only need the decorator for a standalone click command. Commands registered on `app.cli` or `bundle.cli`, or made with `AppGroup.command()` (`src/tessel/cli.py:405`), get wrapped in `needs_app_scope` automatically. You can turn that off with `needs_app_scope=False`.",
